it's very  clearly demonstrated that the those  companies have used and played the need  for housing as a reason to not ask them  to build to higher environmental  standards which we think is terrible and  they should really be held to account it  doesn't cost that much more  there should be an ethical  responsibility on our house builders to  be coming up with designs that stand the  test of time homes we feel proud of  places we want to stay it's not so much  about whether or not you like the look  of that new development down the road  but whether or not enough thought has  gone into how it affects the local  community so that those who move in feel  pulled up by their surroundings rather  than dragged down if we want future  generations to look back and admire what  we've built in the same way we do the  Victorians the Edwardian the Georgians  then design really matters because what  we're building now is a legacy we all  have to live with Katie Spencer Sky News
 

